            <ArticleTitle>Laparoscopic diagnosis and treatment of an infarcted epiploic appendage.</ArticleTitle>
            <Pagination>
                <MedlinePgn>325-7</MedlinePgn>
            </Pagination>
            <Abstract>
                <AbstractText>A patient experienced acute abdominal pain that was diagnosed at laparoscopy as being due to an infarcted epiploic appendage. To our knowledge, this is the second report of laparoscopic diagnosis and treatment of an epipolic disorder. Infarcted epiploic appendages may be associated with bowel obstruction and abscess formation. Therefore, they should be looked for at the time of diagnostic laparoscopy for acute abdominal pain of unclear etiology, and removed if present.</AbstractText>
            </Abstract>
